{"id": "section-body-29844", "title": "Dermatomyositis / Polymyositis", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "RHEUMATOLOGICAL DISORDERS", "Connective Tissue Diseases (CTDs)", "Dermatomyositis / Polymyositis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-29844", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Dermatomyositis / Polymyositis", "runs": [{"text": "Dermatomyositis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "/"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Polymyositis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "105"}}, {"id": "body-29845", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Dermatomyositis (DM) and polymyositis (PM) are inflammatory myopathies causing proximal muscle weakness. DM is marked by distinctive skin rashes (e.g., Gottron’s papules, heliotrope rash), whereas PM lacks skin involvement. Both may lead to significant functional impairment.", "runs": [{"text": "Dermatomyositis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(DM)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "polymyositis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PM)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inflammatory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "myopathies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "proximal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "muscle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weakness."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "DM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "marked by distinctive skin rashes (e.g., Gottron’s papules, heliotrope rash), whereas PM lacks skin involvement. Both may lead to significant functional impairment."}]}, {"id": "body-29846", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Gottron's papules are red or violet, flat-topped, scaly lesions that appear symmetrically over joint extensor surfaces—typically the knuckles, elbows, knees, and ankles", "runs": [{"text": "Gottron's papules are red or violet, flat-topped, scaly lesions that appear symmetrically over joint extensor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surfaces—typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "knuckles,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "elbows, knees, and ankles"}], "images": [{"src": "/data/images/image49.jpeg", "alt": "image49.jpeg"}]}, {"id": "body-29853", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A heliotrope rash is a distinctive reddish-purple or lilac discoloration of the upper eyelids and periorbital region, often associated with DM, an autoimmune inflammatory myopathy.", "runs": [{"text": "A heliotrope rash is a distinctive reddish-purple or lilac discoloration of the upper eyelids and periorbital region, often associated with DM, an autoimmune inflammatory myopathy."}]}, {"id": "body-29856", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4, "images": [{"src": "/data/images/image50.jpeg", "alt": "image50.jpeg"}]}, {"id": "body-29857", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Proximal muscle weakness: Symmetric, gradual onset", "runs": [{"text": "Proximal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "muscle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weakness:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Symmetric,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gradual "}, {"text": "onset"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "105"}}, {"id": "body-29858", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Skin signs (DM only): Heliotrope rash, Gottron’s papules, photosensitive rash", "runs": [{"text": "Skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(DM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "only):"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Heliotrope"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rash,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Gottron’s papules, photosensitive rash"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "105"}}, {"id": "body-29859", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Systemic: Fatigue, fever, weight loss", "runs": [{"text": "Systemic:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fatigue,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "f